lean/ClmVerify/REPORT.md:29:## Theorems ↔ contract items
lean/ClmVerify/REPORT.md:33:| Item | Theorem(s) |
lean/ClmVerify/REPORT.md:50:The checkpoint layout, the padded last segment, the per-cube shared-memory reductions over channels and the parameter-gradient sums are **not** modelled; they are tested against the `f64` reference (`tests/selective_scan.rs`). `chunkedRevScan_eq_revScan` (a three-phase reverse scan) is proven but describes no kernel that exists today; it is what a chunk-parallel backward would rely on.
lean/ClmVerify/REPORT.md:54:| Item | Theorem(s) |
lean/ClmVerify/REPORT.md:65:| Item | Theorem(s) |
lean/ClmVerify/REPORT.md:76:| Leak injection | `not_kept_of_violation`, `not_kept_of_label_reaches_next`, `not_kept_test_of_label_past_end` |
lean/ClmVerify/REPORT.md:82:| Item | Theorem(s) |
lean/ClmVerify/REPORT.md:95:- **Exact algebra, not floats.** Floats are not a semiring because addition is not associative. Chunked = sequential holds exactly in exact arithmetic (checked at `Int` by `clmcheck`); for f32/f64 it holds only up to rounding, so Rust must compare with a tolerance. The same applies to `adjoint_identity`.
lean/ClmVerify/REPORT.md:100:- **`clmcheck backtest`** ignores the calendar end, as specified; `runBacktest_eq_posTrades` links it to the full ledger.
lean/ClmVerify/REPORT.md:101:- **`adjoint`** ignores `u`; `clmcheck` passes `u = 0` (`adjoint_indep_u`).
lean/ClmVerify/REPORT.md:103:None of these weakens a requested theorem.
lean/ClmVerify/REPORT.md:105:## Executable `clmcheck`
lean/ClmVerify/REPORT.md:107:`.lake/build/bin/clmcheck` reads one command per line and answers each with result lines followed by `end`. Bad input gives `error <msg>` then `end`. Blank and `#` lines produce no output.
lean/ClmVerify/REPORT.md:117:Checks: `test/expected.txt` covers chunk sizes 1, n, > n and non-divisible; n = 0; skipped folds; expanding vs rolling; rolling clipped at 0; empty val/cal; `h + e` emptying keep ranges; negative years; malformed commands. A separate Python port of the contract text agreed with `clmcheck` on 3 × 3000 random commands (about 28k lines, about 760 folds).
