docs/reviews/codex_review4_fixes.md:1:1. [finance/crates/clm-cli/src/report.rs:163](/home/user/Documents/workspace/mamba-trainer/finance/crates/clm-cli/src/report.rs:163) — critical — reports do not verify the run signature. `cv` refuses a mismatched resume, but `report` never reads `run.json`. Running `report --config changed.toml --run old-run` can re-backtest old OOF predictions with new costs, policy threshold, labels, or data indexing. Fix: load `run.json` and require its signature to equal `cfg.signature(&Dataset::load(cfg)?.version)` before loading artifacts.
docs/reviews/codex_review4_fixes.md:3:2. [finance/crates/clm-cli/src/data.rs:169](/home/user/Documents/workspace/mamba-trainer/finance/crates/clm-cli/src/data.rs:169) — major — external-prediction provenance remains incomplete. The manifest contains dataset/fold/sample hashes but not the normalizer hash, config/source signature, or external seed. A rebuilt feature/normalization implementation with unchanged bars and split keys accepts stale LightGBM predictions trained on differently normalized inputs. Fix: include and verify a canonical normalizer hash, run/config/source signature, and baseline seed/candidate definition.
docs/reviews/codex_review4_fixes.md:5:3. [src/tensor/ops/selective_scan.rs:136](/home/user/Documents/workspace/mamba-trainer/src/tensor/ops/selective_scan.rs:136) — major — benchmarking overrides can exceed shared-memory limits. `seg_len` budgets staging for default `flush=2`, but `set_backward_flush(Some(8))` and `set_segment_len(Some(8))` permit allocation based on `flush=8` without validation. At `state=32`, the stage alone is 67,584 bytes, above the explicitly capped 48 KiB. Kernel compilation/launch can fail. Fix: validate override combinations against `seg*2*state + flush*2*state*(GROUP+1)` f32 elements, cap/reject unsafe settings, and cap segment overrides to the supported register budget.
