docs/reviews/codex_review1_kernels.md:1:1. [src/tensor/ops/selective_scan.rs:762](</home/user/Documents/workspace/mamba-trainer/src/tensor/ops/selective_scan.rs:762>) — major — stale checkpoints are accepted for unrelated inputs. The check validates only `seg_len` and buffer length. Save checkpoints for `x1`, then call `selective_scan_backward(dy, x2, dt2, a2, bm2, …, Some(&saved1))` with the same shapes; it uses `x1`’s states to differentiate `x2`, producing incorrect `dx`, `ddt`, and parameter gradients. Fix: store and validate input buffer identities/device/shape in `SelectiveScanCheckpoints`, or make checkpoint use private to the autograd path; recompute on any mismatch.
docs/reviews/codex_review1_kernels.md:3:2. [src/tensor/ops/selective_scan.rs:271](</home/user/Documents/workspace/mamba-trainer/src/tensor/ops/selective_scan.rs:271>) and [317](</home/user/Documents/workspace/mamba-trainer/src/tensor/ops/selective_scan.rs:317>) — major — chunked forward does not compose the same floating-point affine transforms as sequential forward. Phase 1 sums `dt` in f32 and phase 2 uses `exp(sum_dt * A)`, rather than multiplying the per-step `exp(dt * A)` factors used by the actual recurrence. For example: `B=D=N=1`, `T=40_000`, `Chunked(20_000)`, `A=-1e-4`, every `dt=0.1`, `Bm*x=1` only at `t=0`, and `Cm=1`: f32 accumulation of `0.1` over a chunk is materially inaccurate, yielding a different carried state in chunk 2 (already beyond the test’s `2e-5` forward tolerance). The current maximum tested `T` is 64. Fix: store/compute each chunk’s per-state multiplier by iteratively multiplying the exact f32 step decay, alongside the local state, then use that multiplier in phase 2.
docs/reviews/codex_review1_kernels.md:5:3. [finance/lean/ClmVerify/ClmVerify/Scan.lean:101](</home/user/Documents/workspace/mamba-trainer/finance/lean/ClmVerify/ClmVerify/Scan.lean:101>) and [finance/lean/ClmVerify/REPORT.md:40](</home/user/Documents/workspace/mamba-trainer/finance/lean/ClmVerify/REPORT.md:40>) — major — the reverse Lean model is not the reverse algorithm implemented by the CubeCL kernel, despite the report saying it models “the kernel … as it runs.” Lean proves a three-phase reverse-chunk algorithm (`revSummarize`/`revCarries`/`chunkedRevScan`), while the kernel at [selective_scan.rs:457](</home/user/Documents/workspace/mamba-trainer/src/tensor/ops/selective_scan.rs:457>) recomputes each *forward checkpoint segment* and performs a sequential right-to-left adjoint carry across those segments. It has no reverse chunk summaries or reverse carries, and it additionally includes checkpoint layout, padded final segments, and tiled shared-memory reductions absent from Lean. The theorem is mathematically useful, but does not verify the implementation described in the report. Fix: either model/prove the checkpointed segment-recomputation backward kernel specifically, or revise REPORT/C7 to describe this as a semantic adjoint model rather than a kernel model.
docs/reviews/codex_review1_kernels.md:7:4. [src/tensor/ops/selective_scan.rs:143](</home/user/Documents/workspace/mamba-trainer/src/tensor/ops/selective_scan.rs:143>) — minor — `SelectiveScanMode::Chunked(usize::MAX)` can overflow `raw.div_ceil(seg) * seg`; in release this can wrap to zero and subsequently panic on `d.seq.div_ceil(chunk)` at line 626. Fix: cap the requested chunk to `seq` before rounding, or use checked arithmetic and return `Error::Config`.
